        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The version of this PR should now be part of the latest `main`.\r\n\r\nIn the end, it seemed like the best design here is to allow users to replace the \"Failed expectation for ...\" text. As this is a bit placeholder-y and might be utilized better by custom message.\r\n\r\nThe new feature can be levered via [`opts.fail_reason`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/19973fa2c13399d68bf8d2cd98b0cb7367a8a72a/doc/mini-test.txt#L553-L555) for all expectations (yes, this required a breaking change for `expect.error` and `expect.no_error`, which is currently somewhat backward-compatible). It can be either a pre-defined string or a function that computes the reason based on expectation's input arguments.\r\n\r\nThanks again for the PR! Hope this redesign still meets your initial idea of the feature.",
